// Title: Microsoft IIS Connection Strings Decryption
// Sigma ID: 97dbf6e2-e436-44d8-abee-4261b24d3e41
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-28 | Modified: 2022-12-30
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003
// Description: Detects use of aspnet_regiis to decrypt Microsoft IIS connection strings. An attacker with
//   Microsoft IIS web server access via a webshell or alike can decrypt and dump any hardcoded
//   connection strings, such as the MSSQL service account password using aspnet_regiis command.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/microsoft-iis-connection-strings-decryption.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_iis_connection_strings_decryption.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\aspnet_regiis.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "aspnet_regiis.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "connectionStrings" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -pdf")
